{
  "title": "ISic001347. Funerary inscription",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\">[ἔζησεν</span> ὁ] <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀντώνιος\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀντώνιος\">[Ἀν]<span data-text=\"τών\">τών</span>[ιος</span></span>  <span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔτη</span> ο´ [<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\">ἔζησεν</span>  <span data-text=\"ὁ\">ὁ</span>  <span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σα\n                    τορνῖλος\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σα\n                    τορνῖλος\">Σ[α-]<br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>τορνῖλος</span></span>  <span data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔ[τη</span>  <span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>  <span data-text=\"τελευτᾷ\">τελ(ευτᾷ)]</span>  <br id=\"al6-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span data-text=\"τῇ\">τῇ</span>  <span data-text=\"πρὸ\">πρ(ὸ)</span> δ´ <span data-text=\"καλανδῶν\">κα[λ(ανδῶν)</span>  <span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\">[......</span>.]<br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀντώνιος\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀντώνιος\">[..]<span data-text=\"τών\">ΤΩΝ</span>[...</span></span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ</span>Ο[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\">ΕΖΗΣΕΝ</span><span data-text=\"ὁ\">Ο</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σα\n                    τορνῖλος\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σα\n                    τορνῖλος\">Σ[.]<br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>ΤΟΡΝΙΛΟΣ</span></span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\">Ε[..</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span><span data-text=\"τελευτᾷ\">....]</span><br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span data-text=\"τῇ\">ΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"πρὸ\">ΠΡ</span>Δ<span data-text=\"καλανδῶν\">ΚΑ[.</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text after IG</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 5\">line.5: <span>ἔ[η IG XIV 528; ἔ[τη CIG IV 9496</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 6\">line.6: <span>l. 6 τῇ πρ(ὸ) δʹ IG XIV 528; τῇ πρ(ὸ) ςʹ CIG IV 9496</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703\">Alex Antoniou</a></p>  <p>Antonios lived [...] for 70 years [...] Satornilos lived for [?] years [... and died] 4 [days] before the Kalends [of...]</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>Both funerary inscriptions are Christian, as suggested also by the attention devoted to recording the exact day of death. Both <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἀντώνιος</span> and <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Σατορνῖλος</span> are names attested in Sicily. For an <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἀντώνιος Σατορνῖλος</span>, see IG XIV 245 (= <a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001063\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001063</a>, from Cava d’Ispica).</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li>cf. ICatania no.12</li><li> Gualtherus 1624 [1625] 102 no. 14 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931</a>  </li><li> Kirchhoff 1877 9496 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249</a></li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">528</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a></li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  </div>",
