      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>Both funerary inscriptions are Christian, as suggested also by the attention devoted to recording the exact day of death. Both <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἀντώνιος</span> and <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Σατορνῖλος</span> are names attested in Sicily. For an <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἀντώνιος Σατορνῖλος</span>, see IG XIV 245 (= <a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001063\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001063</a>, from Cava d’Ispica).</p>  "
